103	 * Pure, and given everything it decides on, because this is the one
104	 * place a run can be moved by something that is not looking at it. Two
105	 * rules do the work. A press names the offer it was drawn from, so one
106	 * made while the unit was closing cannot roll into the next unit. And a
107	 * press names itself, so a deck that pressed twice in a breath, or
108	 * retried after an answer that never arrived, moves the run once.
109	 */
